<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">13 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 13 February, from 1258 to 2008.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1258</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mongols begin the sack of Baghdad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hulagu's troops entered Baghdad and began a week of killing and plunder. Libraries and the city's great institutions of learning were destroyed, and tens of thousands of inhabitants died.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1542</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Catherine Howard is executed at the Tower of London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VIII's fifth wife, still a teenager, was beheaded for adultery and treason. She was the second of his queens to be executed, after her cousin Anne Boleyn.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1633</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo arrives in Rome to face the Inquisition</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Summoned over his 'Dialogue Concerning the Two Chief World Systems', Galileo reached Rome. Tried that spring, he was forced to abjure the view that the Earth moves and spent his last years under house arrest.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1689</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">William III and Mary II offered the English crown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the Banqueting House, the Convention Parliament presented the Declaration of Rights and offered the throne jointly to William and Mary. The settlement limited royal power and confirmed Parliament's role.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1861</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fortress of Gaeta surrenders, ending the Kingdom of the Two Sicilies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a three-month siege by Piedmontese forces, King Francis II surrendered Gaeta and went into exile. Weeks later the Kingdom of Italy was proclaimed under Victor Emmanuel II.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1945</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Allied bombers begin the destruction of Dresden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British and then American raids over two days created a firestorm that killed about 25,000 people and destroyed the historic centre. The attack's justification has been debated ever since.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">2008</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Kevin Rudd apologises to the Stolen Generations</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Australia's Prime Minister delivered a formal apology in Parliament to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people taken from their families under past government policies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></li></ol>
